===Etymology 2===
From the past participle of {{l|enm|mengen||stir up someone's mind}} or formed from [[English]] {{l|en|ming||to bring to (someone's) mind}}. In Middle English, came to mean 'an [[exhortation]]'. In the 17th and 18th centuries attaining a specialized medical sense before becoming obsolete.

